Returns & Refunds Decision Tree Flow

START
  ↓
What do you need help with?
  ├── Return an item
  │     ↓
  │   Do you have your order number?
  │     ├── No → Explain where to find order number → Back to Main Menu
  │     └── Yes → Enter order number
  │                ↓
  │             Order found?
  │                ├── No → Try Again / Back to Main Menu
  │                └── Yes
  │                     ↓
  │             Item in original condition?
  │                ├── No → Not eligible → View Policy / Main Menu
  │                └── Yes
  │                     ↓
  │             Within 30-day return window?
  │                ├── No → Return period expired → View Policy / Main Menu
  │                └── Yes → Eligible → Show return instructions
  │
  ├── Check refund status
  │     ↓
  │   Enter order number → System checks refund
  │     ├── Not Started → Explain processing stage
  │     ├── In Progress → Explain expected processing
  │     ├── Completed → Confirm refund issued
  │     └── Failed → Contact Support
  │
  ├── How long do I have to return?
  │     ↓
  │   Explain 30-day return window and exceptions → View Policy / Main Menu
  │
  └── Other question
        ↓
      Show available returns/refunds options → Contact Support if needed

3. Decision Rules
•	Return eligibility: Order must be found, item must be in original condition, and item must be within the defined return window.
•	Return window: Use 30 days from delivery for the MVP. Northstar should confirm the final production policy before deployment.
•	Refund status: Support at least four states: Not Started, In Progress, Completed, and Failed.
•	Unknown order: Never fabricate order information. Ask the customer to retry or provide a route to support.
•	Fallback: Every branch should provide a way back to the main menu; unresolved issues should offer Contact Support.
4. MVP UX Requirements
•	Use simple buttons/options wherever possible to reduce ambiguous customer input.
•	Keep each response short, clear, and reassuring.
•	Avoid dead ends: every branch should provide a next action.
•	Show Back to Main Menu on appropriate response screens.
•	Provide Contact Support when the decision tree cannot resolve the customer's issue.
•	Do not expose internal system details, database errors, or technical error messages to customers.
